=== demo
pipeline(string): source -> filter(len>=4) -> pool(fan-out, uneven work) -> reorder
  in    12 element(s)
  kept  8 element(s)
  work  8 element(s) through the pool
  link  pool consumed every element the filter emitted
  out   [flow#826923, pipeline#223553, over#826923, bounded#802037, channels#223553, order#760988, comes#760988, back#826923]
pipeline(int): source -> transform(x*3) -> reorder
  link  transform consumed every element the source emitted
  out   [3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18, 21, 24]
reduce(string -> int): commutative fold, no index needed
  sum   54 char(s) over 12 element(s)
  check agrees with the sequential fold
backpressure: a 512-element source into a 4-slot channel
  ring  filled with 4 element(s) and no receiver
  park  send 5 is blocked: no marker for it exists
  drain 512 element(s) and 508 marker(s) after release, producer sent 512
cancel(int): source -> try(step refuses element 8) -> guard closes done
  err   range failed at index 8: value 8 is outside the range this step accepts (0..7)
  stop  the source produced fewer than 256 element(s): cancellation reached the head of the pipeline
  join  both stages returned; the checker saw every element the source sent
graph(string): a Plan built, then run -- filter(len>=4) + stamp, reassembled by index
  plan  words: filter then work, ring of 8
  in    12 element(s), 8 through the plan
  out   [flow#826923, pipeline#223553, over#826923, bounded#802037, channels#223553, order#760988, comes#760988, back#826923]
graph(string): the same Plan run fallibly over 768 elements, cancelled at the first refusal
  err   plan failed at index 3: word 'pipeline' is longer than this step accepts (7)
  stop  the source produced fewer than 768 element(s): the plan's first refusal reached the head of the pipeline
  join  both stages returned; the plan saw no more than the source sent
errors: every FlowErr variant, fired
  ok    duplicate index 0: the index set is not a permutation
  ok    truncated: expected 3 item(s), collected 2
  ok    filter dropped 2: 9 sent, 7 received
